{
  "_comment": [
    "MEASUREMENT FIXTURE — every R4 Questionnaire.item.type, used to re-walk the CSP ladder against the whole",
    "producer contract instead of the group/boolean subset the original measurement used.",
    "",
    "It DELIBERATELY carries the two types that DEGRADE, so the degradation stays MEASURED rather than assumed,",
    "and so the fixture doubles as live proof that unrenderableQuestionnaireFeatures() reports them.",
    "",
    "MEASURED IN THE WEB WORKBENCH 2026-08-17 (both differed from the prediction, and both matter because the",
    "control LOOKS answerable while being permanently blank — a reviewer reads that as an unanswered question):",
    "  reference — predicted 'no widget'. Actually renders an empty TEXT INPUT that can never hold the",
    "              valueReference answer. _getDataType has no `reference` case, so it returns the initializer",
    "              \"string\", which is not an LForms dataType (ST is).",
    "  url       — predicted to render normally. The control renders, but the answer never populates:",
    "              _lformsTypesToFHIRFields maps URL -> \"Url\", so LForms reads valueUrl, and R4",
    "              QuestionnaireResponse.item.answer has no valueUrl (R4 uses valueUri).",
    "",
    "Everything else rendered and populated correctly, including the coded items that pull the autocompleter",
    "PNGs — no CSP violation, and nothing reached LForms' 6-second JSONP icon loader.",
    "",
    "The attachment answer carries real base64 image data on purpose: that is the only path by which an",
    "attachment could ask the renderer for an image preview, and img-src deliberately excludes data:.",
    "",
    "R4 defines a 17th code, `question`, which is abstract and not for use. It is excluded on purpose.",
    "",
    "No answerValueSet, no preferredTerminologyServer, no answerExpression, no x-fhir-query: those need a",
    "terminology server or FHIR context that this pane does not configure, and connect-src is shut."
  ],
